  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collaborative  response to  losses and damages related to Climate change.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide group cash transfer to 15 groups who will use the funds to address the different losses and damages related to climate change. It will also support  four water infrastructure rehabilitation that were affected due to climate related impacts to ensure access to water for both human and livestock use. Conflicts over resources  increase during droughts and this project will work with the different communities along the boarders to promote peace and coexistence, sharing of resource even during calamities.  Oxfam and PGI  with  funding from SIDA RRM  HPA III Yr 4 (24 -25) will deliver an integrated lifesaving response reaching 7,920 individuals, 5076 located in Tana River and 2844 in Garissa, who have been impacted by sudden onset crisis caused by flooding. The response will focus on vulnerable mixed populations, which include internally displaced persons (IDPs)  particularly those recently on the move, as well as host communities, through a needs -based approach.   The integrated response includes interventions focused on cash to access to basic needs, safe water and sanitation facilities, as well as protection measure through a gender sensitive approach. This integrated response ensures a wholistic intervention to meet the urgent lifesaving needs of affected communities, maximizing the impact and effectiveness.   The most significant impact of the project lies in the immediate access to food, clean water and protection services for 780 vulnerable households through multi -purpose cash assistance (MPCA), and the urgent reactivation of 20 community -based protection committees to strengthen protection mechanisms and facilitate referrals for survivors of violence and abuse during an onset crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
